{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786209977,"nonce":"TRmdrr7fQFPUsZlQDUjzvYKwADs=","title":"**What is wrong.** Across twelve modules there is exactly one test under an `api`","message":"package: `internal/sources/api/sources_guard_test.go`. Nothing tests the handlers\nfor alerts, alert groups, occurrences, notifications, policies, deliveries,\nchannels, silences, stats, streaming or identity — 71 declared operations, 36 of\nwhich a human once exercised by hand in an audit that has not been repeated and\ncannot be.\n\n**Why it matters.** Every finding in the conformance audit lived in this layer:\n`getVersion` returning no `{data,meta}` envelope, `/readyz` with the wrong shape,\n`delivery_summary` missing two required members, a `NotificationReason` the server\nemits and the contract rejects, SSE headers never sent. The audit's own verdict\nwas \"the causal chain is one link long: *nothing has ever checked*. Every\nC-finding is the kind a single smoke test would have caught on the day it was\nwritten.\" Those specific bugs are fixed; the layer that produced them is still\nunguarded, so the next eight are already being written.\n\n**Where.** `internal/*/api/` (handlers, DTOs, mappers, routers),\n`api/openapi/openapi.yaml` as the assertion target.\n\n**Done when.** Every operation in `openapi.yaml` has at least a happy-path\n`httptest` case asserting status and response shape against the schema, plus the\n403/404/412/422 branch where the handler has one; validation failures assert the\n`violations[]` field and code; and the tenant-scoping probe (another org's id →\n404, never another tenant's data) is a test rather than a one-off audit script.","files":null}]}